{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_80", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/sh -lc \"cat > /tmp/research_history/episode_4_continuing_draft.md <<'MD'\n# Continuing research notes: episode 4\n\n## Fully evaluated results so far\n| Variant | Raw seconds | Score | Quality | Exact evaluator source hash |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n|136_all_torch_reductions|.0735952235995986|.8588763515055424|all30 valid|f6fb552bc2afd0b84bb2daa3a8d912d159992a8d9604b98d8f396fa402bfe60c|\n|145_inplace_matrix_scaling|.06843345973272032|.8687743708868532|all30 valid|1da84d688b4a1dde5586eb23b05e48769639b4f0b56931b8bbb9d6a92b1a6492|\n|162_precomputed_norm_geometry|.06487423613192125|.8755994146299784|all30 valid|f57def419ac069782eeb981cefb9157e8d2a80d927c6794c0cd116203a4b37a6|\n|165_addmm_baddbmm_geometry|pending|pending|localall30 valid|pending official report|\n\nStarting best123 raw .07845975276820051, score .8495482990735561.162 improves measuredraw17.315% from episode start. No canonical baseline timing re-estimated; formalB=.5214946210980997 from prior evaluator score formula. All reported evaluator logs and result.json files copied unchanged from exact printed result paths. Preserve exact hashes.\n\n## Recipe changes from123\n- Coupling matrix scaling algebra: normalizeK columns to1/m, then rows to1/n, twice. Final energy sum(K*C). These are exactly the same alternating steps as dualvectorSinkhorn, up to float32 rounding, and eliminate contiguous transpose copies/matvec overhead. Broadcoupling remains dense and array-derived.\n- Vectorize100 classpair featurebounding boxes and repeated padded featurefill to avoid100 separateTorch reductions/assignments. Original100 empirical crossclass costs and schedules retained.\n- Reuse feature norm vectors across all point batchpairs; directly calculateT=.5||a||²+.5||b||²-a dotb with in-place mm arithmetic. Add empirical labelcostW/2. Both coupling and dual share this geometry.\n- MutateC only after its last use: final pointtransform subtractsg in place; final class residualsubtractsf andg in place. Suppliedfeaturearrays are never modified.\n- Replace denseexp with scaledexp2 for coupling and direct dualfallback: exp(z)=exp2(z*log2e). All30 gates pass, numerical differences negligible within recorded float32 approximation.\n-165 further fusesfeature geometry withaddmm andclass geometry withbaddbmm. Retain only if fourth official report beats162.\n- Retains from123: twoTorchthreads, flushdenormalflag before threadpool; sharedresidual exponential kernel recurrence with reciprocalrow/column factors and two squares at quartertemperatures; omit unnecessary kernelmaxnormalization with relativepositive-mass stabilitychecks and dense fallback. Initialfullsofttransform, coarse2skip, late3pointskip, classhardmin<=8, pointhardmin<=2, finalpoint hardmin .1. Same contiguous1024batches, scalarNewton outer3x2transport at reg.01; otherreferencebatchcounts usePOT.\n\n## Experiments and decisions\n-126vectorizedclasssetup,127firstgeometryreuse,128globalgeometry,129packedclassgeometry,130/131in-placecoupling energy/mass: all30localvalid, accuracy~.0039615. Sharingfeaturegeometryforclasscost correct but gather/copy overhead offsets speed. Globalgeometry sometimes faster but exactempirical class setup still more efficient measured162.\n-132onecouplingiteration fails6/30, worst .0117195863.133initialcolumnsum andcalibratedrowenergy,134stridedtranspose,135weightedcolumnreduce,136allTorchreductions all30pass.136formal selectednewbest.\n-137NumPypoint,138NumPyclass,139both: all30pass butslower.140unpadded segmentedclasssolver sortsobservedclasssupports, operatesononecrossmatrix andNumPyreduceat; accurateall30 butfreshmedian .16799 vs136 .07630. Rejectspeed. No supports dropped.\n-141globalgeometry+reductions,142vectorizedsetup+reductions,143singlepow4,144base2exp,145in-placebalancing,146streamedhardreductions: all30pass. Pow4 muchslower thantwosquares.145formalnewbest.146doesnot changeoutput andlittle benefit beca