computed by the saved canonical initial source, not protected targets. These screens are not scores. `fresh_bench.py` runs eight fresh processes per variant in alternating order. First paired round1 overlapped a local screen and is marked diagnostic; subsequent fresh rounds had no concurrent numerical work. Official evaluations had no concurrent numerical workloads.\n-Only public inputs and local canonical calculations used. No protected targets, evaluator source, private inputs, other trajectories, credentials, environment variables, network or subagents accessed. No protected assets or frozen launcher changed.\n-For a fresh episode, start from the exact measured best. Profile it before choosing the next bottleneck. Remaining point-dual kernel recurrence and class symmetric transforms likely dominate. Possible next hypothesis: group class pairs by support size while retaining Torch contiguous reductions, reducing padding and dense working sets. The full NumPy segmented solver and Taylor compression were slower; repeating them is unlikely useful. Public nRMSE margin is about .006.\n'\"'''\nPath('/tmp/research_notes.md').write_text(notes)\n(root/'episode_4_continuing_notes.md').write_text(notes)\np=root/'episode_4_working_notes.md';p.write_text(p.read_text()+'\\\\n165 fourth full official result '+json.dumps(r)+'. Exact report copied unchanged. Final measured best '+best+' restored.\\\\n')\n(root/'episode_4_final_selection.json').write_text(json.dumps({'best':best,'raw_metric':report['raw_metric'],'score':report['score'],'method_sha256':report['method_sha256'],'worst_nrmse':worst,'min_spearman':rho,'min_top':top},indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint(json.dumps({'best':best,'raw_metric':report['raw_metric'],'score':report['score'],'method_sha256':report['method_sha256'],'latest':r},indent=2))\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
